# Example. Copy to `.graphifyignore` and own it.
# bkit install does not write this file and does not overwrite a copy.
# graphify corpus scope. Same syntax as .gitignore.
# .gitignore is read automatically and merged with this file; patterns here are
# evaluated last and only ever exclude more. Everything already ignored by
# .gitignore (node_modules/, dist/, migration/, *.csv, tmp/, .worktrees/) needs
# no entry here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Everything an LLM would have to read.
#
# graphify parses code locally with tree-sitter and never calls a model for it.
# Docs, PDFs, images, office files and video are the ONLY paths that reach a
# backend. `--code-only` skips them per run, but that flag is per-invocation and
# there is no persistent equivalent — .graphifyrc supports only viz_node_limit
# and no GRAPHIFY_CODE_ONLY env var exists. Excluding the file types here makes
# the corpus structurally code-only, so a bare `graphify extract .` or
# `/graphify .` has nothing to send even without the flag.
#
# Counts at time of writing: 4148 .md, 52 .png, 27 .html, 22 .yaml/.yml, 8 .pdf,
# 7 .txt, 5 .jpg/.jpeg, 2 .xlsx, 2 .docx. `*.md` alone leaves 125 files behind.
*.md
*.mdx
*.qmd
*.rst
*.txt
*.html
*.yaml
*.yml
*.pdf
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.gif
# graphify's image detection is wider than the extensions its README lists.
# With only the four documented types excluded, a run still reported
# "7 non-code file(s) (0 docs, 0 papers, 7 images)" — 3 .svg, 2 .heic, 2 .avif.
# The rest of the raster set is listed so the guarantee survives someone
# committing a .bmp rather than breaking silently.
*.svg
*.heic
*.avif
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.ico
*.heif
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mp3
*.wav

# Four binary image fixtures (photo.heic / photo.avif under
# packages/services/src/inbound/__fixtures__/attachments/ and
# apps/run/docling/benchmark/corpus/) still appear on the extract's
# "skipping N non-code file(s)" line and do NOT respond to any ignore rule,
# including excluding their directory outright. That counter is computed before
# ignore filtering for the image class; graphify's source contains no reference
# to "heic" or "avif", so it classifies them from the OS mime database. They
# never enter manifest.json, so nothing reads them. Do NOT exclude those two
# directories to zero the counter — both contain real TypeScript (corpus.ts,
# expected.ts, manifest.ts) and dropping them costs 23 code nodes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Agent harness — config, hooks and tool state, not application code.
# Left in, these contributed ~450 nodes and dominated the god-node ranking:
# .opencode/opencode.json alone yielded 112 nodes and .claude/settings.json 71.
# .serena/ self-ignores only its cache and project.local.yml, so the rest of it
# is visible to graphify; it is another agent's working state either way.
.agents/skills/
.bkit/
.claude/
.codex/
.cursor/
.opencode/
.serena/

# Generated plan and design artefacts. The markdown is already covered above;
# this line is for the 27 .json and 59 .jsonl files under the same tree, which
# graphify treats as code.
docs/plans/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Build and tooling JSON. `.json` is a code extension to graphify, so these
# are parsed as source and every top-level key becomes a node with no manifest
# semantics behind it — 206 nodes of task and env-var names for turbo.json,
# whose `globalEnv` key ranks as a god node at 41 edges when parsed.
#
# package.json is NOT excluded, and must never be. graphify reads the workspace
# `name` fields out of the CORPUS to resolve a workspace package specifier;
# excluding package.json silently destroys cross-package resolution. Measured on
# this repo with identical tsconfigs: 104 cross-package edges over 4 package
# pairs with it excluded, 217 over 35 with it present. It is worth the two noise
# nodes it costs (`scripts` and `test`, the JSON keys shared by 22 workspaces).
#
# tsconfig.json IS excluded and that is safe — graphify reads tsconfig `paths`
# whether or not the file is in the corpus. Verified by A/B: identical
# cross-package edge counts either way.
**/turbo.json
**/tsconfig.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT excluded: apps/web/e2e/ (321 nodes) and **/*.test.ts. They
# are real code with real call edges, and dropping them would blind the
# `graphify affected` blast-radius query to its test callers.
